{
  "description": "The conformance table of the wire validator every runtime carries: one family's wire description, one imported family's, and cases of a type expression, a JSON value, and whether the value is valid. The imported family's envelope carries the trace context and the meta every injected envelope carries, so that a slot of it is held to accepting traceparent, tracestate and a flat map of strings, and to refusing any of them at another type. The reserved nightseam. prefix of a meta key is the peer's rule and no facet of the type, so a reserved key passes the slot here and the frame carrying it is refused by the peer; tables/frames.json holds that. Both runtimes read this file. A type drawn from a parameter is not among the cases: the TypeScript validator holds it to the binding of the parameter and the Go validator passes it through, since a generated Go codec validates it where the generic type is instantiated; each runtime tests its own way.",
